// A #module cycle: cycle_a imports cycle_b, which imports back cycle_a.
// Neither file is reachable on its own (module_compile() only ever
// starts from an importer), so the cycle only surfaces once something
// outside it imports in, here. Both live directly alongside this file
// (not under fixtures/, unlike this directory's other error tests)
// because a module's declared #moduledef name has to match every one of
// its importers' own reference string, and cycle_a is imported both by
// this file and by its sibling cycle_b; putting all three in the same
// directory is what lets every reference use the same unprefixed name.
// Intentionally never expected to compile; see module_errors.pw for the
// general convention this otherwise follows.

#module "cycle_a"

fn main() {
}
